Open Router2 → **CLI** tab, press Enter, then paste this:

```
enable
configure terminal
interface g0/0
 ip address 10.0.2.2 255.255.255.252
 no shutdown
interface g0/1
 ip address 10.0.4.2 255.255.255.252
 no shutdown
interface g0/2
 ip address 192.168.1.1 255.255.255.0
 no shutdown
exit
router ospf 1
 network 10.0.2.0 0.0.0.3 area 0
 network 10.0.4.0 0.0.0.3 area 0
 network 192.168.1.0 0.0.0.255 area 0
end
write memory
```

All routers are now configured. Next:

1. Set the PC IPs (PC0 192.168.0.10, PC1 192.168.1.10, masks 255.255.255.0, gateways .1).
2. On Router0, run `show ip ospf neighbor` (two FULL neighbors) and `show ip route ospf` (two equal-cost routes to 192.168.1.0/24).
3. Then apply `ip ospf cost 100` on Router0 g0/0 and re-check the route.
